    description: "Found while measuring the 2026-08-15 module_completeness audit (PR #361), not while looking for it. Small - 6 calls of 1898 - and filed anyway because the population it belongs to is the one _is_analyzed_module was written to empty, and a gate that leaks its own repo's modules is reporting blindness about code it read. Poetry was the original measurement behind that branch: 120 of 171 call-site modules were poetry's own, so the branch carries real weight and a leak in it is worth understanding rather than absorbing. Do NOT fix by adding a prefix rule - a prefix rule over module names was measured wrong in three languages at once (see _module_matches); establish the actual matching shape first."  # 905f
    fields:  # 905f
      statement: "A module whose source this analysis read is not a catalogue gap: _is_analyzed_module exists to exclude it, because whatever I/O it performs was examined on its own edges. VIOLATED: hypergumbo_core, hypergumbo_core.scip._generated and hypergumbo_lang_mainstream.py.EXTERNAL_CONSTRUCTOR_TYPES appear in the uncatalogued-module set on hypergumbo's own self-survey, all three first-party."  # 905f
      root_cause: "Unmeasured. _is_analyzed_module compares a call-site module against the set of modules the analysis produced symbols for; the three names that leak are all DOTTED forms that name a first-party module plus a submodule or an attribute (…scip._generated, …py.EXTERNAL_CONSTRUCTOR_TYPES), so the likely cause is the same exact-vs-component matching question that INV-fokik and the os.environ slot mismatch both turn on - but that is a hypothesis, not a measurement."  # 905f
